# Kairos backend settings. Copy to backend/.env for local runs (git-ignored), or paste the values into your
# host's "Environment" settings (Render / Railway / Fly). NEVER commit a real value. Every line is optional:
# with an empty file the backend runs fully, on mock channels, with no AI models.
# Lines starting with "# NAME=" are optional: remove the "# " and fill in a value to use one.

# ── AI models (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One Sarvam key powers sarvam-prism (decisions), sarvam-105b-conversations (WhatsApp phrasing) and
# deepseekv4.1-flash-1017 (summaries). Get it from the Sarvam dashboard → API keys. Starts with sk_.
SARVAM_API_KEY=
# Turn every model off without removing the key: off
# KAIROS_SARVAM_MODELS=
# Subset of features: prism,voice,phrasing,narrative (default: all four)
# KAIROS_SARVAM_FEATURES=

# ── Secrets the backend uses internally ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any long random string, e.g.  python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
# Signs CM-03 OTPs. Without it each process makes its own random key (fine for one instance).
# KAIROS_CM03_SECRET=
# Salts the hashed borrower ids in K26 reports.
# KAIROS_REPORT_SALT=
# Hashes email addresses in the email channel.
# KAIROS_EMAIL_HASH_KEY=

# ── Storage ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SQLite files (defaults: backend/kairos.db and the churn engine's own file). On free hosts the disk resets on
# every deploy or restart, which is fine for the demo: everything is synthetic and re-seeded.
# KAIROS_DB=
# KAIROS_CHURN_DB=
# Policy folder (default: ../policy from backend/)
# KAIROS_POLICY_DIR=

# ── Demo behaviour ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Channels: mock (default, nothing is sent). Keep mock for any public deployment.
KAIROS_CHANNELS=mock
# Show the OTP that CM-03 "sent" in its console (synthetic +910 numbers only): 1
KAIROS_CM03_DEMO_INBOX=1
# Send free-text replies through the intent stack: 1
# KAIROS_INTENT_STACK=
# Database refuses undeclared state changes: 1
# KAIROS_FSM_STRICT=
# Seconds between automatic churn ticks (0 = off)
# KAIROS_TICK_INTERVAL_S=0

# ── Webhook protection (only if a real provider calls this server) ─────────────────────────────────
# Sarvam voice webhooks must send header X-Kairos-Webhook-Secret with this value.
# SARVAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Meta WhatsApp Cloud API: webhook verify token and app secret (signature check), plus sending credentials.
# WA_VERIFY_TOKEN=
# WA_APP_SECRET=
# WA_TOKEN=
# WA_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=

# ── Real sends: leave OFF for any shared or public deployment ───────────────────────────────────────
# Phone-demo adapters (send to an allow-list of your own numbers, kept outside the repo). Dry-run unless set.
# KAIROS_DEMO_SMS=
# KAIROS_DEMO_WHATSAPP=
# KAIROS_DEMO_ANDROID_SMS=
# KAIROS_DEMO_ALLOWLIST=
# KAIROS_DEMO_RECIPIENTS_FILE=
# Email sandbox (SMTP)
# KAIROS_SMTP_SANDBOX=
# KAIROS_SMTP_HOST=
# KAIROS_SMTP_PORT=
# KAIROS_SMTP_USER=
# KAIROS_SMTP_PASSWORD=
# KAIROS_SMTP_FROM=
# KAIROS_SMTP_ALLOWED_DOMAINS=
